From d171b1d97c1e9a20929dd386b0f5ed869e9cac7b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DoubleGate <parobek@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 01:54:32 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] [UPSTREAM] analysis: inter-RAT downgrade detector (T-OR-057)

RatDowngradeAnalyzer (default off) flags a network-directed move off LTE
toward a legacy/sunset RAT, complementing the broadcast-reselection
analyzers (priority_2g_downgrade for SIB6/7, connection_redirect_downgrade
for a Connection Release redirect):

- MobilityFromEUTRACommand with a CellChangeOrder to 2G/GERAN -> High
  (an explicit, per-UE directed downgrade off LTE).
- MobilityFromEUTRACommand with a Handover purpose -> Informational
  (legitimate inter-RAT handovers exist).
- An LTE cell advertising CDMA2000 reselection via SIB8 -> Low (anomalous
  in markets where CDMA2000 is decommissioned; legitimate where it runs,
  so a per-MCC sunset policy to raise it is future work).

Stateless; keys on the message/IE alone. Off by default pending per-market
calibration. Tests use TS 36.331 vectors encoded with the reference Python
pycrate and decoded here through telcom_parser (two independent ASN.1
implementations): a CellChangeOrder-to-GERAN command, a SIB8 broadcast, and
a benign RRCConnectionReconfiguration that must not fire.

